  {
    "number": 58,
    "title": "Render the actual Lines layout with animated Prism crystal components",
    "body": "The wall now draws the saved Nanoleaf arrangement with the approved Prism crystal components. Hexagonal connectors and full-thickness tubes assemble outward in about two seconds. Task-active Lines send two independently colored packets from their connectors to a center spark on the shared two-second UI rhythm.\n\nImplements #53, following the verified connector source in #52 / PR #56. The same scalable material is used throughout assembly and the final pose. Work, Quiet, Free, reduced motion, polling, geometry replacement, selection, keyboard focus, project/task associations, explicit Locate and browser-local playback preferences retain their app contracts. Invalid connector geometry retains the last valid wall or the standard map on first load. The renderer disposes its observers, input listeners and frames.\n\nThe approved archive fingerprint is recorded with reproducible SVG component exports. Runtime JavaScript is served only through two explicit local asset paths. Existing source/upgrade copy lists include those assets; no device, scene, task epoch, tray, service or installed-state behavior changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The full local browser suite passes at runtime/test revision `2e40b35311573cae5b89c2b027e9cf905a0dab72`. It retains all 360 raw number clicks and foundation journeys, and checks two-zone colors/half swaps, transformed endpoint ownership, mechanical poses, the 50 ms flow continuity boundary, keyboard focus after valid replacement, malformed/unsupported/first-load fallback, interaction passivity, reduced motion, host visibility and repeated renderer cleanup. Document visibility uses an explicit hidden-state event simulation; host visibility uses the browser's IntersectionObserver.\n- Chromium headless shell 149.0.7827.55 ran the suite through the documented executable override. Desktop, compact, mobile and 2× pixel-density assembly captures were produced. Desktop and mobile captures were inspected; human approval of this current implementation is still required.\n- At 1440×1000, DPR 1, upper glow and active Work, 120 frame intervals measured 33.3 ms median / 33.4 ms p95 for the actual 15-Line, 12-connector layout. The documented 56-Line triangular-lattice fixture measured 83.3 ms median / 100 ms p95. These measurements describe this machine and do not establish a 300-Line performance envelope.\n- Five pure adapter/component tests pass. The 161-test Python suite passes for the unchanged server/packaging implementation, including the copied foreground Linux package smoke test and bounded asset/security tests. Component export is reproducible.\n- Current workflow validation passes with seven specifications, seven complete archives and ten workflow tests. `gh-53-prism-renderer` is synchronized and archived. The final commit changes only specification bookkeeping and packaging documentation after the passing browser revision.\n\n## Remaining delivery gates and handoffs\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews will use this PR's fixed base/head. All nine configured hosted jobs must pass for the reviewed head. GitHub stopped the preceding run before any job started with an account billing/spending-limit error; local browser results do not replace hosted CI. Human approval of the current integrated UI, guarded merge, main CI and issue readback remain pending. Do not auto-close #53.\n\nThe luminous-number visibility and neighbour-clearance refinement is #26 and follows this renderer. [Linux PR #57](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/57), owned under #54, must copy `prism.js` and `prism-adapters.js` beside the wall source when reconciling these branches. Its Python-only runtime glob does not include JavaScript. This PR does not take over that installer.\n\nGuide synchronization remains pending in [Hub PR #82](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/82). No installation, physical-light acceptance or public guide publication is claimed.\n",
    "state": "open",
